      "citation": "Measured from address to the top, then top to impact. Published tour figures are measured from the TAKEAWAY instead, so this metric reads a little higher than the 3:1 benchmark and a band cut for that basis sits slightly low for this one -- by the (small, structurally bounded, so far UNMEASURED) Address->Takeaway gap. Provisional until re-centred on a corpus. NB the low-side Watch band is empty: 1.8 is exactly -2 sigma, so a rushed transition goes Good -> Action at 1.8. Deliberate for now; revisit with the literature review."
    },
    {
      "measure": "m_leadWristAtImpact",
      "context": "full_swing",
      "mu": 15.0,
      "sigmaLo": 12.0,
      "unit": "°",
      "source": "heuristic",
      "citation": "Migrated from the swing scorer's own impact band (pp_tuned_constants.h kFlexExtMu = 15.0, kFlexExtSigma = 12.0), which grades the ABSOLUTE sample at impact and is locked against HackMotion in Corpus 2. The scorer penalises only BELOW mu (cupping), which is exactly what sig_scooping detects; the two-sided corridor here is the conservative reading of the same figure. NB the sibling delta reduction (m_leadWristFlexExt_p7, the wrist-grid cell) carries mu 8.0, while this metric's howToRead implies a delta near 22.5 — see C1 in the implementation plan. That disagreement is about the DELTA and does not touch this absolute row."
    },
